+A CPU-only isolated bootstrap waits for the start command until the supervisor has assigned its retained process handle to a Windows Job Object and verified the actual interpreter PID belongs to it. This handles Windows virtualenv redirectors without attaching arbitrary external PIDs. The noninheritable Job handle has KILL_ON_JOB_CLOSE and no breakaway. Shutdown, load/request timeouts, startup errors and supervisor crash clean up the owned process tree. Containment failure refuses startup before model imports. A failed or abandoned mutex requires revalidation/operator restart; no automatic reload loop occurs. The retained-handle adapter uses CPython Windows subprocess internals and must be revalidated when Python changes.
